Optimal Flow Matching (OFM) [2]. The authors of [2] propose OFM method, an adaptation of FM to solve the OT problem. They restrict the domain of FM loss minimization only to optimal vector fields which are typical for the solutions of the dynamic OT or the Benamou-Brenier problem. These fields are defined by convex functions Ψ: initial point z0 at t = 0 moves to ∇Ψ(z0) at t = 1, and intermediate point xt, t ∈ (0, 1) lies on the straight line between z0 and ∇Ψ(z0):
